## 1. Acceptance

You receive rights under this license only if you accept and comply with all of
its terms. These terms are conditions of every license granted below.

## 2. Scope

"Software" means the OpenVoiceFlow source code, object code, documentation, and
other material distributed with this license, but not any material identified
as third-party or separately licensed.

"Covered Work" means the Software, a modified version of the Software, or a work
that incorporates, links to, imports, adapts, translates, or is otherwise based
on any copyrightable part of the Software. Merely communicating with the
Software through a documented operating-system or network interface, without
incorporating or modifying the Software, does not by itself create a Covered
Work.

"Integration" means any software, configuration, plugin, adapter, workflow, or
service intentionally designed to connect to, control, extend, or exchange data
with the Software. An Integration may be an independent work and may not be a
Covered Work when it merely communicates with an unmodified build through a
documented interface. Even then, the attribution condition in Section 5 applies
to the Integration.

"Organization" means any employer, client, business, institution, association,
organized group, nonprofit, educational or charitable entity, public-interest
entity, or government entity, whether for-profit or nonprofit and whether paid
or unpaid.

Each contributor licenses only the material for which that contributor has the
right to grant a license. Earlier releases and separately identified portions
remain governed by the license notices that accompany them.

## 3. Permitted purpose: personal use only

Subject to the source-sharing conditions below, a natural person may use, copy,
modify, and distribute the Software solely for that person's own personal use.
Personal use includes research, experiment, testing, personal study, private
entertainment, hobby projects, amateur pursuits, or religious observance for
your own benefit, without anticipated commercial or organizational application.

Personal use does not include use by, for, or on behalf of any Organization. A
use is not personal merely because no money changes hands.
Only personal use as defined in this section is permitted under this public
license.

## 4. Commercial and organizational use are not granted

This license does not permit commercial or organizational use. Organizational
use means use by, for, or on behalf of any Organization. Commercial use
includes, without limitation:

- using the Software, a Covered Work, or an Integration for work, business
  operations, an employer, a client, or a commercial organization;
- offering or using it in a paid product, paid service, hosted service,
  monetized workflow, advertising-supported activity, or revenue-generating
  activity;
- selling, sublicensing, renting, leasing, bundling, reselling, or commercially
  distributing it; or
- using it where procurement, paid support, warranty, indemnity, or other
  commercial terms are required.

Commercial or organizational rights require separate written permission or a
separate written license from Shimoverse Studios. Contact `contact@openvoiceflow.com`.

### 4.1 Grace period while permission is requested

If you begin a commercial or organizational use in good faith and send a written
request to `contact@openvoiceflow.com`, you may continue that use for thirty days
after sending the request, or until Shimoverse Studios responds, whichever is
later. This grace period applies once per organization, not once per person, and
does not waive the attribution and source-sharing conditions in Section 5. If
permission is declined, you must stop the commercial or organizational use
within thirty days of that response.

## 5. Attribution and source-sharing conditions

If you create a Covered Work or Integration—including a fork, derivative, or
modified version—you must preserve this license and all copyright, attribution,
and third-party notices. You must also state prominently **"Based on
OpenVoiceFlow by Shimoverse Studios"** and provide a working link to the original
source code at <https://github.com/shimoverse/openvoiceflow> in its source README
and, if it has an About screen, user documentation, or other credits location,
in that location as well. This attribution requirement applies whether or not
you distribute it, provide network access to it, or the Integration is a Covered
Work.

### 5.1 Distribution

If you distribute or otherwise provide a Covered Work to anyone, you must, at
no charge:

1. provide the complete Corresponding Source to every recipient at the same
   time, or provide a durable written offer and working URL from which every
   recipient can obtain it;
2. make that Corresponding Source publicly available from a stable URL without
   registration, payment, or access restrictions;
3. license the entire Covered Work and its Corresponding Source under this exact
   license, without additional terms that restrict the rights granted here;
4. preserve and display the notices and attribution required by this Section 5
   in locations reasonably visible to recipients and users;
5. state prominently that you changed the Software, identify the material
   changes, and provide the date of each release; and
6. use a name and branding that do not imply the Covered Work is an official
   OpenVoiceFlow release, except to state truthfully that it is based on
   OpenVoiceFlow.

The public source must remain available for as long as you distribute the
Covered Work and for at least three years after your last distribution.

### 5.2 Network use

If you modify the Software or create a Covered Work and allow anyone other than
you to interact with its functionality over a computer network, you must make
the complete Corresponding Source publicly available under the conditions in
Section 5.1 no later than the first day that network access is provided. The
user interface or service documentation must include a reasonably prominent
"Source" link to that public source and the attribution required by Section 5.

Using an unmodified official OpenVoiceFlow build solely as a local personal tool
does not trigger this network-use condition merely because optional text cleanup
contacts a third-party model provider.

### 5.3 Corresponding Source

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for making changes to the
Covered Work, including all source code, interface definitions, scripts,
configuration, dependency manifests, and build and installation instructions
reasonably necessary to generate, install, and run the same Covered Work. It
does not include unmodified third-party dependencies that are normally obtained
from their original public sources, but their names, versions, and applicable
licenses must be disclosed.

You may charge only the reasonable direct cost of physically transferring a
copy. You may not use access controls, contracts, or technological measures to
prevent recipients from exercising rights granted by this license for a
permitted purpose.

